## 3. Dataset and model

- **Dataset:** [BloodMNIST](https://medmnist.com/) (MedMNIST v2) – 17,092 microscope images of blood cells, 28×28 RGB, **8 classes** (basophil, eosinophil, erythroblast, immature granulocytes, lymphocyte, monocyte, neutrophil, platelet). Official split: 11,959 train / 1,712 validation / 3,421 test.
- **Licence:** CC BY 4.0. Citation: J. Yang et al., *MedMNIST v2 – A large-scale lightweight benchmark for 2D and 3D biomedical image classification*, Scientific Data, 2023. ⚠️ Research/education only – **not for clinical use**.
- **Task:** multi-class image classification.
- **Training:** Google Colab (T4 GPU) – [`model/bloodmnist_training.ipynb`](model/bloodmnist_training.ipynb). Reproducible: fixed seed 42, pinned [`model/requirements.txt`](model/requirements.txt), official test set never used for model selection (best epoch and best model chosen on the validation set by macro-F1).

### Results on the test set (3,421 images)

| Model | Accuracy | Macro-F1 |
|---|---|---|
| Baseline 1 – most frequent class | 0.195 | 0.041 |
| Baseline 2 – PCA (100) + logistic regression | 0.774 | 0.744 |
| Small CNN (from scratch, ~0.3 M params) | 0.970 | 0.968 |
| **ResNet-18 fine-tuned (ImageNet weights) – selected** | **0.971** | **0.969** |
| Final ONNX export (same predictions) | 0.971 | 0.969 |

Macro-F1 is reported because the classes are imbalanced (accuracy alone would hide weak small classes). Confusion matrix: [`docs/confusion_matrix.png`](docs/confusion_matrix.png).

### Exported model

| | |
|---|---|
| File | `model/model-1.0.0.onnx` (semantic version **1.0.0**) |
| Size | 44.7 MB (< 100 MB) |
| CPU latency (1 thread) | **5.5 ms mean, 6.3 ms p95** (< 1 s) |
| Input | `image` float32 `(batch, 3, 28, 28)` in [0, 1] – resize + normalisation are **inside** the ONNX graph |
| Output | `probabilities` float32 `(batch, 8)` – softmax inside the graph |
| Contract | [`model/input_schema.json`](model/input_schema.json) (shared by the dispatcher and the API) |

