## 6. Event-driven pipeline (`/functions`)

One Flex Consumption Function App, Python 3.12, v2 programming model, three functions:

| Function | Trigger | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `dispatcher` | Event Grid (`BlobCreated` on `input/`) | checks **extension** (.png/.jpg/.jpeg), **size** (≤ 1 MB, not empty), **schema** (really a PNG/JPEG, 8–4096 px). Valid → message to `inference-requests`. Invalid → copy to `rejected/` + `<name>.reason.json` |
| `worker` | queue `inference-requests` | **idempotent** (id = SHA-256 of blob name + ETag; skips if already in Cosmos; upsert write), reused HTTP client with **timeout**, calls `/predict`, writes `output/<name>.json` and the metadata to Cosmos DB, emits metrics |
| `recent` | HTTP `GET /api/recent` | last 20 inferences, CORS restricted to the dashboard origin |

### Example Event Grid event (input of the dispatcher)

```json
{
  "topic": "/subscriptions/<sub>/resourceGroups/rg-projet-bcellaj/providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/stbcellajpipe",
  "subject": "/blobServices/default/containers/input/blobs/neutrophil_0.png",
  "eventType": "Microsoft.Storage.BlobCreated",
  "eventTime": "2026-11-20T12:55:54.000Z",
  "data": {
    "api": "PutBlob",
    "contentType": "image/png",
    "contentLength": 1782,
    "blobType": "BlockBlob",
    "eTag": "0x8DF47059185DE59",
    "url": "https://stbcellajpipe.blob.core.windows.net/input/neutrophil_0.png"
  },
  "dataVersion": "", "metadataVersion": "1"
}
```

### Example queue message (dispatcher → worker)

