## 9. Deployment – step by step

Prerequisites: Azure for Students subscription (owner), Azure Cloud Shell (Bash), GitHub account. Full commented script: [`infra/`](infra/).

```bash
# 0. Variables (Cloud Shell forgets them when it restarts: paste again each session)
EQ=bcellaj; LOC=francecentral; RG=rg-projet-$EQ; ST=st${EQ}pipe; COSMOS=cosmos-$EQ
ENV=cae-$EQ; FUNC=func-$EQ; ID=id-github-$EQ; LAW=log-$EQ; AI=appi-$EQ

# 1. Region checks + providers (section 3.2 of the subject)
az policy assignment list --disable-scope-strict-match --query "[?contains(displayName,'region') || contains(displayName,'location')].parameters" -o json
az functionapp list-flexconsumption-locations -o table

# 2. Resource group (tags) and Cosmos DB FIRST (Free Tier, CLI)
az group create -n $RG -l $LOC --tags projet=dscc equipe=$EQ
az cosmosdb create -n $COSMOS -g $RG --enable-free-tier true --locations regionName=$LOC failoverPriority=0 isZoneRedundant=False
az cosmosdb sql database create -a $COSMOS -g $RG -n pipeline --throughput 400
az cosmosdb sql container create -a $COSMOS -g $RG -d pipeline -n inferences --partition-key-path /fileName

# 3. Storage: containers, queues, versioning, static website
az storage account create -n $ST -g $RG -l $LOC --sku Standard_LRS --kind StorageV2 --min-tls-version TLS1_2 --allow-blob-public-access false
az storage account blob-service-properties update -n $ST -g $RG --enable-versioning true
for c in input output rejected models; do az storage container create --account-name $ST -n $c; done
az storage queue create --account-name $ST -n inference-requests
az storage queue create --account-name $ST -n inference-requests-poison
az storage blob service-properties update --account-name $ST --static-website --index-document index.html

# 4. Monitoring (capped workspace + App Insights) BEFORE the apps
az monitor log-analytics workspace create -g $RG -n $LAW -l $LOC --quota 0.2
az monitor app-insights component create --app $AI -g $RG -l $LOC --workspace $(az monitor log-analytics workspace show -g $RG -n $LAW --query id -o tsv)

# 5. Container Apps environment + API (image built by ci.yml, public on GHCR)
az containerapp env create -n $ENV -g $RG -l $LOC --logs-workspace-id <customerId> --logs-workspace-key <key>
az containerapp create -n api-$EQ -g $RG --environment $ENV --image ghcr.io/apira1899/bloodcell-pipeline/api:1.0.0 \
  --target-port 8000 --ingress external --cpu 0.25 --memory 0.5Gi --min-replicas 0 --max-replicas 2 \
  --secrets appinsights-conn="<connection string>" --env-vars APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING=secretref:appinsights-conn
#    + liveness/readiness probes on /health (az rest PATCH of the template)

# 6. Function App (Flex Consumption) + identity + roles + settings + code
az functionapp create -n $FUNC -g $RG --storage-account $ST --app-insights $AI --flexconsumption-location $LOC --runtime python --runtime-version 3.12 --instance-memory 512
az functionapp identity assign -n $FUNC -g $RG        # then the 3 role assignments (section 6)
az functionapp config appsettings set -n $FUNC -g $RG --settings STORAGE_ACCOUNT_URL=... PIPELINE_STORAGE__queueServiceUri=... API_URL=... COSMOS_ENDPOINT=...
az functionapp deployment source config-zip -g $RG -n $FUNC --src functions.zip --build-remote true

# 7. Event Grid -> dispatcher (only after the code is deployed)
az eventgrid event-subscription create -n blob-to-dispatcher --source-resource-id <storage id> --endpoint-type azurefunction \
  --endpoint <function app id>/functions/dispatcher --included-event-types Microsoft.Storage.BlobCreated \
  --subject-begins-with /blobServices/default/containers/input/

# 8. Dashboard + CORS
az storage blob upload --account-name $ST -c '$web' -f web/index.html -n index.html --content-type text/html
az functionapp cors add -n $FUNC -g $RG --allowed-origins https://stbcellajpipe.z28.web.core.windows.net

# 9. GitHub OIDC identity (Contributor on the resource group only)
az identity create -n $ID -g $RG
az identity federated-credential create -n github-production-ids --identity-name $ID -g $RG \
  --issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  --subject "repo:Apira1899@132703325/bloodcell-pipeline@1465266331:environment:production" --audiences api://AzureADTokenExchange
az role assignment create --role Contributor --assignee-object-id <principalId> --assignee-principal-type ServicePrincipal --scope <resource group id>

# 10. Alert (action group + log alert every 15 min) and budget ($25, alerts 20/50/80 %)
```

