## 10. Azure for Students restrictions encountered and solutions

| Restriction / problem | What we saw | Solution applied |
|---|---|---|
| Only 5 allowed regions | policy `listOfAllowedLocations` | Chose `francecentral` (allowed + Flex Consumption + closest) |
| Cosmos DB: portal may offer only EUAP regions | – | Created Cosmos DB **first, with the CLI**, in `francecentral`: Free Tier accepted |
| No Entra ID rights (no service principal) | – | GitHub → Azure through a **user-assigned managed identity + federated credential (OIDC)** |
| **OIDC subject mismatch** `AADSTS700213` | GitHub now sends `repo:Apira1899@132703325/bloodcell-pipeline@1465266331:environment:production` (immutable owner/repo IDs) | Added a federated credential with **the exact subject printed by `azure/login`** |
| ACR Tasks unavailable / ACR costs ≈ $0.17/day | – | Image built in GitHub Actions and pushed to **GHCR** (free, public) |
| Static Web Apps often outside allowed regions | – | Dashboard hosted in the storage **`$web` static website** |
| One Container Apps environment only | – | Single environment `cae-bcellaj` |
| Contributor cannot assign roles | – | Role assignments created once by the subscription owner; GitHub identity = Contributor on the group only |
| Python 3.12 runtime on Flex Consumption | remote build failed: `azure-functions==2.4.0` requires Python ≥ 3.13 | Pinned `azure-functions==1.26.0` |
| Cloud Shell is ephemeral | variables lost after each disconnection (`expected one argument` errors) | Variables block kept in a text file and pasted at the start of every session |
| CLI extensions prompt (Y/n) in Cloud Shell | a hidden prompt blocked a command | `az config set extension.use_dynamic_install=yes_without_prompt` |
| A budget named `budget-dscc` already existed in the subscription | – | Created `budget-bcellaj` scoped to the project resource group |
| $100 credit shared with all courses | – | Budget $25 + alerts 20/50/80 %, App Insights cap 0.2 GB/day, scale to zero, deletion after the defence |

